# Normalise line endings in the repository, and pin them per file type on
# checkout. This is not cosmetic: Git for Windows defaults to
# core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites every text file to CRLF on checkout. A
# CRLF install.sh run under Git Bash or WSL fails with
#   bash: install.sh: /usr/bin/env^M: bad interpreter
# and a CRLF shell script inside a GitHub Actions ubuntu runner fails the same
# way. Most Rain World players are on Windows, so this file is what keeps the
# Linux/macOS path working for a contributor who cloned on Windows.

*               text=auto eol=lf

# Must stay LF regardless of platform: interpreted by bash or by a Linux runner.
*.sh            text eol=lf
*.py            text eol=lf
*.yml           text eol=lf
*.yaml          text eol=lf

# Must be CRLF: PowerShell 5.1, which is what ships with Windows and what most
# users will run install.ps1 under, mis-parses some multi-line constructs when
# the file is LF-only and saved without a BOM.
*.ps1           text eol=crlf
*.bat           text eol=crlf
*.cmd           text eol=crlf

# Never touched.
*.png           binary
*.jpg           binary
*.dll           binary
*.pdb           binary
*.zip           binary

# Keep generated/vendored noise out of diffs and out of the language stats.
refs/**         binary linguist-vendored
CHANGELOG.md    merge=union
